  "description": "DAVNOH crystallizes in the rhombohedral crystal system with space group R -3. Reported CIF formula moiety: C84 H66 N6 O78 Sm12,6(H2 O1). From the CIF bond table, Sm1 (Sm) has 8 O neighbors; Sm2 (Sm) has 8 O neighbors; Sm1P (Sm) has 8 O neighbors; Sm2P (Sm) has 8 O neighbors; Sm1Q (Sm) has 8 O neighbors; Sm2Q (Sm) has 8 O neighbors; Sm1A (Sm) has 8 O neighbors; Sm2A (Sm) has 8 O neighbors; Sm1B (Sm) has 8 O neighbors; Sm2B (Sm) has 8 O neighbors; Sm1O (Sm) has 8 O neighbors; Sm2O (Sm) has 8 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 12 pairs, 1 components; largest component is a network with cycles with three-dimensional metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.674-3.846 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 102.31-108.67°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula [Sm12(HL)6(L)6(NO3)6(H2O)12]·6H2O. Explicit grouped units in the article formula/name: 6 NO3 (explicit grouped unit in article formula), 12 H2O (explicit grouped unit in article formula).",
  "interpretation_limit": "Oxidation states, nuclearity, oxo/hydroxo bridging, core charge and ligand identities/counts require article/SI or manual verification; atom-site counts are asymmetric-unit counts, not molecular stoichiometry. Graph topology is limited to identity-symmetry bonds in the CIF table. Approximate shape is based only on bridge-unwrapped metal-site coordinates in the largest component; symmetry-related bonds or periodic structures require manual crystallographic review. Empirical formulas alone do not establish unique oxidation-state assignments or ligand connectivity; annotations above reproduce explicit structural notation only.",
